Firefox 157.0.1: decode with Vulkan Video on a device that cannot export a dma-buf.

shared_vulkan docs/video-decode.md §7.7, docs/design.md §0.21.9 tier 1.

FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder has two output paths and both end in vkGetMemoryFdKHR.
A forwarded Vulkan device decodes on the far side of a VM boundary and has no
descriptor to give, so this adds a third, behind
media.hardware-video-decoding-vulkan.readback.enabled (default false):

- av_hwframe_transfer_data (loaded beside av_hwframe_map) copies the decoded
  NV12 frame to host memory and VideoData::CreateAndCopyData makes the same
  PlanarYCbCrImage the software decoder makes; no dma-buf, no sync_fd. Any
  other format is a DECODE_ERR, which MediaFormatReader recovers from with
  software decode, so 10-bit falls back instead of failing.
- InitCtx (the dma-buf copy ring, which needs the export entry points) is not
  run in readback mode.
- GfxInfo probes the Vulkan device even when the GL test calls the GL
  "software": Vulkan decode does not use GL, and Zink on a device with no DRM
  node is reported as software by Mesa's EGL.

- gfxPlatformGtk drops HARDWARE_VIDEO_DECODING's "Requires DMABUF" when the Vulkan
  decoder is enabled with readback: those frames are never DMA-BUFs.

Applies to the nixpkgs firefox-unwrapped 157.0.1 source with -p1.

